question:
Hebu $n$ iwe nambari kamili chanya. Weka $a_{n,0}=1$. Kwa kila $k\geq 0$, chagua kwa bahati nasibu nambari kamili $m_{n,k}$ kutoka kwenye seti $\{1,\,\ldots,\,n\}$ kwa uwezekano sawa, kisha weka
\[
a_{n,k+1}=\begin{cases} 
a_{n,k}+1, & \text{ikiwa $m_{n,k}>a_{n,k}$;}\\[6pt]
a_{n,k}, & \text{ikiwa $m_{n,k}=a_{n,k}$;}\\[6pt]
a_{n,k}-1, & \text{ikiwa $m_{n,k}<a_{n,k}$.}
\end{cases}
\]
Iwe $E(n)$ ni thamani tarajiwa ya $a_{n,n}$. Bainisha $\lim_{n\to\infty}E(n)/n$.

translated_en:
Let $n$ be a positive integer. Set $a_{n,0}=1$. For each $k\geq 0$, randomly select an integer $m_{n,k}$ from the set $\{1,\,\ldots,\,n\}$ with equal probability, then set
\[
a_{n,k+1}=\begin{cases} 
a_{n,k}+1, & \text{if $m_{n,k}>a_{n,k}$;}\\[6pt]
a_{n,k}, & \text{if $m_{n,k}=a_{n,k}$;}\\[6pt]
a_{n,k}-1, & \text{if $m_{n,k}<a_{n,k}$.}
\end{cases}
\]
Let $E(n)$ be the expected value of $a_{n,n}$. Define $\lim_{n\to\infty}E(n)/n$.

question:
Kwa nambari isiyo hasi ya jumla \( n \) na mfuatano wa namba halisi zinazoongezeka kikamilifu \( t_0, t_1, \ldots, t_n \), iwe \( f(t) \) ni funge halisi inayolingana, iliyofafanuliwa kwa \( t \geq t_0 \) na yenye sifa zifuatazo:
(a) \( f(t) \) ni endelevu kwa \( t \geq t_0 \), na inaweza kutofautishwa mara mbili kwa \( t > t_0 \) isipokuwa katika nukta \( t_1, \ldots, t_n \);
(b) \( f(t_0) = 1/2 \);
(c) \( \lim_{t \rightarrow t_k^{+}} f'(t) = 0 \) kwa \( 0 \leq k \leq n \);
(d) Kwa \( 0 \leq k \leq n-1 \), tunayo \( f''(t) = k+1 \) iwapo \( t_k < t < t_{k+1} \), na \( f''(t) = n+1 \) kwa \( t > t_n \).

Kwa kuzingatia chaguo zote za \( n \) na \( t_0, t_1, \ldots, t_n \) zinazoridhisha \( t_k \geq t_{k-1}+1 \) kwa \( 1 \leq k \leq n \), ni thamani gani ndogo zaidi inayowezekana ya \( T \) ambayo \( f(t_0 + T) = 2023 \)?

translated_en:
For a non-negative integer \( n \) and a sequence of perfectly increasing real numbers \( t_0, t_1, \ldots, t_n \), let \( f(t) \) be a corresponding real closed function, defined for \( t \geq t_0 \) and having the following properties:
(a) \( f(t) \) is continuous for \( t \geq t_0 \), and is doubly differentiable for \( t > t_0 \) except at the point \( t_1, \ldots, t_n \);
(b) \( f(t_0) = 1/2 \);
(c) \( \lim_{t \rightarrow t_k^{+}} f'(t) = 0 \) for \( 0 \leq k \leq n \);
(d) For \( 0 \leq k \leq n-1 \), we have \( f''(t) = k+1 \) if \( t_k < t < t_{k+1} \), and \( f''(t) = n+1 \) for \( t > t_n \).

Given all choices of \( n \) and \( t_0, t_1, \ldots, t_n \) that satisfy \( t_k \geq t_{k-1}+1 \) for \( 1 \leq k \leq n \), what is the smallest possible value of \( T \) for which \( f(t_0 + T) = 2023 \)?

question:
Ikiwa $T$ ni seti ya namba zote tatu $(a,b,c)$ za nambari chanya ambazo zinaweza kuunda pembetatu zenye urefu wa pande $a,b,c.$ Eleza thamani ya \[
\sum_{(a,b,c)\in T}\frac{2^a}{3^b5^c}
\] kama namba ya kimahesabu katika umbo lake rahisi kabisa.

translated_en:
If $T$ is the set of all three positive integers $(a,b,c)$ that can form a triangle with side lengths $a,b,c.$ Express the value of \[
\sum_{(a,b,c)\in T}\frac{2^a}{3^b5^c}
\] as a mathematical number in its simplest form.

question:
Tafuta nambari ndogo zaidi chanya ya kitufe $n$, ili iwezekane kupaka kila kisanduku katika gridi ya ukubwa $n \times n$ kwa rangi nyekundu, njano au bluu ambayo inatimiza masharti yote yafuatayo:  
(1) Idadi ya visanduku vilivyopakwa kila rangi ni sawa;  
(2) Ikiwa mstari mlalo una kisanduku chekundu, basi mstari huo lazima uwe pia na kisanduku cha bluu na hauwezi kuwa na kisanduku cha njano;  
(3) Ikiwa safu wima ina kisanduku cha bluu, safu hiyo lazima iwe pia na kisanduku chekundu lakini haiwezi kuwa na kisanduku cha njano.

translated_en:
Find the smallest positive integer $n$, such that it is possible to paint every cell in a grid of size $n \times n$ with red, yellow, or blue that satisfies all of the following conditions: 
(1) The number of cells painted with each color is the same; 
(2) If a horizontal row contains a red cell, then that row must also contain a blue cell and cannot contain a yellow cell; 
(3) If a column contains a blue cell, that column must also contain a red cell but cannot contain a yellow cell.

